cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use RUBLI in research or reporting, please cite it as below. Risk scores are indicators for prioritising investigation, not findings of wrongdoing."
title: "RUBLI: open corruption-risk indicators for Mexican federal procurement"
abstract: >-
  RUBLI ingests Mexican federal procurement records (CompraNet, 2002-2025, and
  post-CompraNet ComprasMX awards), resolves vendors and institutions, scores
  each contract with a statistical risk indicator (model v0.8.5, an ElasticNet
  logistic regression with positive-unlabelled correction), and ranks vendors
  into an investigation queue. Code is Apache-2.0; derived data is CC BY 4.0.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "RUBLI project"
    email: rubli-project@proton.me
    website: "https://rubli.xyz"
  - alias: rodanaya
repository-code: "https://github.com/rodanaya/rubli"
url: "https://rubli.xyz"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-02"
keywords:
  - public procurement
  - corruption risk
  - Mexico
  - CompraNet
  - open data
  - investigative journalism
  - entity resolution
  - positive-unlabelled learning
